G301.b:
⟪Ἀμώς⟫, ὁ indecl. (Heb. ⁨אָמוֹץ⁩, ⟦Isaiah 1:1|Is 1:1⟧; ⁨עָמוֹס⁩, ⟦Amos 1:1|Am 1:1⟧; ⁨אָמוֹן⁩, ⟦2 Kings 21:18|IV Ki 21:18⟧ ff. B);
⟪1.⟫ as in ⟦2 Kings 21:18|IV Ki 21:18⟧ ff. B (Α. Ἀμμών; Jos., Ἀμμών, Ἄμωσσς), ⟪Amon⟫: ⟦Matthew 1:10|Mt 1:10⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪Amos⟫: ⟦Luke 3:25|Lk 3:25⟧.†

G302.b:
⟪ἄν⟫, conditional particle, which cannot usually be separately translated in English, its force depending on the constructions which contain it (see further, LS, s.v.; WM, §xlii; M, Pr., 165 ff.; MM, VGT, s.v.).
⟪1.⟫ In apodosis,
	⟪(i)⟫ c. indic, impf. or aor., expressing what would be or would have been if (εἰ c. impf., aor. or plpf.) some condition were or had been fulfilled: ⟦Luke 7:39|Lk 7:39⟧ ⟦Luke 17:6|17:6⟧, ⟦John 5:46|Jo 5:46⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:10|Ga 1:10⟧, ⟦Matthew 12:7|Mt 12:7⟧ ⟦Matthew 24:43|24:43⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:8|I Co 2:8⟧, ⟦Acts 18:14|Ac 18:14⟧, ⟦1 John 2:19|I Jo 2:19⟧, al. The protasis is sometimes understood (as also in cl.): ⟦Matthew 25:27|Mt 25:27⟧, ⟦Luke 19:23|Lk 19:23⟧. In hypothetical sentences, expressing unreality, ἄν (as often in late writers, more rarely in cl.) is omitted: ⟦John 8:39|Jo 8:39⟧ ⟦John 15:24|15:24⟧ 19:11, ⟦Romans 7:7|Ro 7:7⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:15|Ga 4:15⟧;
	⟪(ii)⟫ c. opt., inf., ptcp. (cl.; v. LS, s.v.; M, Int., §275; M, Pr., 167:4).
⟪2.⟫ In combination with conditional, relative, temporal, and final words;
	⟪(i)⟫ as in cl., c. subj.,
		⟪(a)⟫ in protasis with εἰ, in Attic contr. ἐάν, q.v.;
		⟪(b)⟫ in conditional, relative, and temporal clauses (coalescing with ὅτε, ἐπεί, etc.; v.s. ὅταν, ἐπάν, etc.), ⟪ever, soever⟫;
			⟪(α)⟫ c. pres., ἡνίκα, ⟦2 Corinthians 3:15|II Co 3:15⟧; ὃς ἄν, ⟦Romans 9:15|Ro 9:15⟧(LXX) ⟦Romans 16:2|16:2⟧, al.; ὅσοι ἄν, ⟦Luke 9:5|Lk 9:5⟧; ὡς ἄν, ⟦Romans 15:24|Ro 15:24⟧ (M, Pr., 167);
			⟪(β)⟫ c. aor., ὃς ἄν, ⟦Matthew 5:21|Mt 5:21⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:22|22⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:31|31⟧; ἕως ἄν, ⟪until⟫, ⟦Matthew 2:13|Mt 2:13⟧, ⟦Mark 6:10|Mk 6:10⟧, al.; ὡς ἄν, ⟪as soon as⟫ (M, Pr., 167), ⟦1 Corinthians 11:34|I Co 11:34⟧, ⟦Philippians 2:23|Phl 2:23⟧. On the freq. use of ἐάν for ἄν with the foregoing words, v.s. ἐάν;
	⟪(ii)⟫ in late Gk., when some actual fact is spoken of, c. indic.: ὅταν (q.v.); ὅπου ἄν, ⟦Mark 6:56|Mk 6:56⟧ (M, Pr., 168); καθότι ἄν, ⟦Acts 2:45|Ac 2:45⟧ ⟦Acts 4:35|4:35⟧; ὡς ἄν, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:2|I Co 12:2⟧.
⟪3.⟫ in iterative construction, c. impf. and aor. indic. (M, Pr., 167): ⟦Acts 2:45|Ac 2:45⟧ ⟦Acts 4:35|4:35⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:2|I Co 12:2⟧.
⟪4.⟫ c. optat., giving a potential sense to a question or wish: ⟦Acts 8:31|Ac 8:31⟧ ⟦Acts 26:29|26:29⟧.
⟪5.⟫ Elliptical constructions: εἰ μή τι ἄν (M, Pr., 169), ⟦1 Corinthians 7:5|I Co 7:5⟧; ὡς ἄν, c. inf., ⟪as it were⟫ (op. cit. 167), ⟦2 Corinthians 10:9|II Co 10:9⟧.

G303.b:
⟪ἀνά⟫ prep. (the rarest in NT; M, Pr., 98; MM, VGT, s.v.), prop., ⟪upwards⟫, ⟪up⟫, always c. acc.
⟪1.⟫ In phrases: ἀ. μέσον, ⟪among⟫, ⟪between⟫, c. gen., ⟦Matthew 13:25|Mt 13:25⟧, ⟦Mark 7:31|Mk 7:31⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 6:5|I Co 6:5⟧ (M, Pr., 99), ⟦Revelation 7:17|Re 7:17⟧ [so in LXX for ⁨בְּתוֹךְ⁩]; ἀ. μέρος, ⟪in turn⟫, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:27|I Co 14:27⟧ (both found in Polyb.; cf. MGr. ἀνάμεσα).
⟪2.⟫ Distrib., ⟪apiece, by⟫: ⟦Matthew 20:9|Mt 20:9-10⟧, ⟦Luke 9:3|Lk 9:3⟧ (WH om.), ⟦Luke 9:14|Lk 9:14⟧ ⟦Luke 10:1|Lk 10:1⟧, ⟦John 2:6|Jo 2:6⟧, ⟦Revelation 4:8|Re 4:8⟧.
⟪3.⟫ Adverbially ("a vulgarism," Bl., § 51, 5; cf. Deiss., BS, 139 f.), ἀ. εἷς ἕκαστος, ⟦Revelation 21:21|Re 21:21⟧. As prefix, ἀ. signifies
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪up⟫: ἀναβαίνειν;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to⟫: ἀναγγέλλειν;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪anew⟫: ἀναγεννᾶν;
⟪(d)⟫ ⟪back⟫: ἀνακάμπτειν.†

G331.b:
† ⟪ἀνάθεμα⟫, -τος, τό
(< ἀνατίθημι), Hellenistic for Attic ἀνάθημα (Bl., § 27, 2);
⟪1.⟫ prop. = τὸ ἀνατιθέμένον, ⟪that which is laid by⟫ to be kept, ⟪a votive offering⟫ (as ἀνάθημα in II Mac 2:13, ⟦Luke 21:5|Lk 21:5⟧—where LT read -θεμα, v. M, Pr., 46).
⟪2.⟫ [As equiv. in LXX for ⁨חֵרֶם⁩,] ⟪devoted, a thing devoted to God⟫ (v. Driver, De., 98 f., and cf. ⟦Leviticus 27:28|Le 27:28-29⟧), hence;
	⟪(a)⟫ of the sentence pronounced (⟦Deuteronomy 13:15|De 13:15⟧), ⟪a curse⟫: ⟦Acts 23:14|Ac 23:14⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of the object on which the curse is laid, ⟪accursed⟫ (⟦Deuteronomy 7:26|De 7:26⟧): ⟦Romans 9:3|Ro 9:3⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:3|I Co 12:3⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 16:22|16:22⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:8|Ga 1:8⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:9|9⟧ (v. ICC on Ro.; Lft., ⟦Galatians 1:8|Ga., 1:8⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:9|9⟧; Cremer, 547; Tr., Syn., § v; MM, VGT, s.v.).†

G337.b:
⟪ἀν-αιρέω⟫, -ῶ
[in LXX for ⁨הרג⁩ hi., ⁨מֵת⁩ hi., ⁨נכה⁩ hi., etc.;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to take up⟫: mid., ⟦Acts 7:21|Ac 7:21⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to take away⟫, ⟪make an end of⟫, ⟪destroy⟫ (for late exx. of various senses, v. MM, VGT, s.v.);
	⟪(a)⟫ of things (as freq. in cl. of laws, etc.): ⟦Hebrews 10:9|He 10:9⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of persons, ⟪to kill⟫: ⟦Matthew 2:16|Mt 2:16⟧, ⟦Luke 22:2|Lk 22:2⟧ ⟦Luke 23:32|23:32⟧, ⟦Acts 2:23|Ac 2:23⟧ ⟦Acts 5:33|5:33⟧, ⟦Acts 5:36|36⟧ ⟦Acts 7:28|7:28⟧ ⟦Acts 9:23|9:23-24⟧, ⟦Acts 9:29|29⟧ ⟦Acts 10:39|10:39⟧ ⟦Acts 12:2|12:2⟧ ⟦Acts 13:28|13:28⟧ ⟦Acts 16:27|16:27⟧ ⟦Acts 22:20|22:20⟧ ⟦Acts 23:15|23:15⟧, ⟦Acts 23:21|21⟧ ⟦Acts 23:27|23:27⟧ ⟦Acts 25:3|25:3⟧ ⟦Acts 26:10|26:10⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:8|II Th 2:8⟧, WH, txt., R, txt.†

G352.b:
⟪ἀνα-κύπτω⟫
[in LXX: ⟦Job 10:15|Jb 10:15⟧ (⁨נָשָׂא רֹאשׁ⁩), Da LXX, Su 35*;] ⟪to lift oneself up⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ bodily; ⟦Luke 13:11|Lk 13:11⟧, ⟦John 8:7|Jo 8:7⟧, ⟦John 8:10|10⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ mentally, ⟪to be elated⟫: ⟦Luke 21:28|Lk 21:28⟧ (cf. MM, VGT, s.v.).†

G386.b:
⟪ἀνά-στασις⟫, -εως, ἡ
(< ἀνίστημι), [in LXX: ⟦Zephaniah 3:8|Ze 3:8⟧ (⁨קוּם⁩), ⟦Lamentations 3:63|La 3:63⟧ (⁨קִימָה⁩), ⟦Psalms 66:1|Ps 64 (66) tit.⟧, ⟦Daniel 11:20|Da LXX 11:20⟧, II Mac 7:14 12:43*;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪a raising up⟫, ⟪awakening⟫, ⟪rising⟫ (in Inscr. of the erection of a monument, v. MM, VGT, s.v.): ⟦Luke 2:34|Lk 2:34⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪a rising from the dead⟫ (v. DCG, ii, 605b);
	⟪(a)⟫ of Christ: ⟦Acts 1:22|Ac 1:22⟧ ⟦Acts 2:31|2:31⟧ ⟦Acts 4:33|4:33⟧, ⟦Romans 6:5|Ro 6:5⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:10|Phl 3:10⟧, ⟦1 Peter 3:21|I Pe 3:21⟧; ἐξ ἀ. νεκρῶν, ⟦Romans 1:4|Ro 1:4⟧ (ICC, in l.); ἐκ νεκρῶν, ⟦1 Peter 1:3|I Pe 1:3⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of persons in OT hist. (e.g. ⟦1 Kings 17:17|III Ki 17:17⟧ ff.): ⟦Hebrews 11:35|He 11:35⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ of the general resurrection: ⟦Matthew 22:23|Mt 22:23⟧, ⟦Matthew 22:28|28⟧, ⟦Matthew 22:30|30⟧, ⟦Mark 12:18|Mk 12:18⟧, ⟦Mark 12:23|23⟧, ⟦Luke 20:27|Lk 20:27⟧, ⟦Luke 20:33|33⟧, ⟦Luke 20:36|36⟧, ⟦John 11:24|Jo 11:24⟧, ⟦Acts 17:18|Ac 17:18⟧ ⟦Acts 23:8|23:8⟧ ⟦Acts 24:15|24:15⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 2:18|II Ti 2:18⟧; ἀ. ἐκ νεκρῶν, ⟦Luke 20:35|Lk 20:35⟧, ⟦Acts 4:2|Ac 4:2⟧; τῶν νεκρῶν, ⟦Matthew 22:31|Mt 22:31⟧, ⟦Acts 17:32|Ac 17:32⟧ ⟦Acts 23:6|23:6⟧ ⟦Acts 24:21|24:21⟧ ⟦Acts 26:23|26:23⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:12|I Co 15:12⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 5:13|13⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:21|21⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:42|42⟧, ⟦Hebrews 6:2|He 6:2⟧; ἀ. ζωῆς, resurrection to life (cf. II Mac 7:14, ἀ. εἰς ζωήν) and ἀ. τ. κρίσεως, r. to judgment, ⟦John 5:29|Jo 5:29⟧; ἀ. τ. δικαίων, ⟦Luke 14:14|Lk 14:14⟧; κρείττων ἀ., ⟦Hebrews 11:35|He 11:35⟧; on ἡ ἀ. ἡ πρώτη, ⟦Revelation 20:5|Re 20:5⟧, ⟦Revelation 20:6|6⟧, v. Swete, in l., Westc. on Jo 5, but v. also Thayer, s.v.; by meton. of Christ as Author of ἀ., ⟦John 11:25|Jo 11:25⟧ (v. DB, iv, 231; Cremer, 307).†

G387.b:
† ⟪ἀνα-στατόω⟫, ῶ
(< ἀνάστατος, driven from home; < ἀνίστημι), [in LXX: ⟦Daniel 7:23|Da 7:23⟧ (⁨דּוּשׁ⁩;* also in Aq., and in π. (v. Deiss., LAE, 80 f.; MM, VGT, s.v.),] ⟪to stir up⟫, ⟪excite⟫, ⟪unsettle⟫: c. acc.;
⟪(a)⟫ to tumult and sedition: ⟦Acts 17:6|Ac 17:6⟧ ⟦Acts 21:38|21:38⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ by false teaching: ⟦Galatians 5:12|Ga 5:12⟧ (v. Milligan, NTD, 73 f.).†
